### IPP-402 Questions management API (admin) tests
### How to use: run `npm run dev` in /server, then click "Send Request" above each request, top to bottom.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000/api

### Admin login: put ADMIN_PASSWORD from server/.env here. Put it back to CHANGE_ME after testing.
@adminEmail = askedin143@gmail.com
@adminPassword = CHANGE_ME

### PHP language id (from 401 tests)
@phpId = 6ad894999dcf1f882fd249b2

### Picked up automatically from the requests below
@adminToken = {{adminLogin.response.body.data.token}}
@qaId = {{newQa.response.body.data.question._id}}
@mcqId = {{newMcq.response.body.data.question._id}}


### 1. Admin login -> expect 200
# @name adminLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{adminEmail}}",
  "password": "{{adminPassword}}"
}


### 2. Add WITHOUT login -> expect 401 "Please log in to continue"
POST {{baseUrl}}/admin/questions
Content-Type: application/json

{}


### 3. Add with empty body -> expect 400 with a list of errors
POST {{baseUrl}}/admin/questions
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}


### 4. Add a Q&A -> expect 201 "Question added", tags saved in small letters
# @name newQa
POST {{baseUrl}}/admin/questions
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "language": "{{phpId}}",
  "type": "qa",
  "question": "TEST (IPP-402): What does the null coalescing operator ?? do in PHP?",
  "answer": "It returns the left value if it exists and is not null, otherwise the right value.",
  "difficulty": "easy",
  "tags": ["Operators", "PHP7"],
  "codeSnippet": "$name = $_GET['name'] ?? 'Guest';"
}


### 5. MCQ with only 3 options -> expect 400 "MCQ must have exactly 4 options, none empty"
POST {{baseUrl}}/admin/questions
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "language": "{{phpId}}",
  "type": "mcq",
  "question": "TEST: Which one is a PHP superglobal?",
  "answer": "$_GET holds query string values.",
  "options": ["$_GET", "$GET", "_GET"],
  "correctOption": 0
}


### 6. MCQ with the same option twice -> expect 400 "MCQ options must all be different"
POST {{baseUrl}}/admin/questions
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "language": "{{phpId}}",
  "type": "mcq",
  "question": "TEST: Which one is a PHP superglobal?",
  "answer": "$_GET holds query string values.",
  "options": ["$_GET", "$_get", "_GET", "GET$"],
  "correctOption": 0
}


### 7. MCQ without a correct option -> expect 400 "Choose the correct option (0 to 3)"
POST {{baseUrl}}/admin/questions
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "language": "{{phpId}}",
  "type": "mcq",
  "question": "TEST: Which one is a PHP superglobal?",
  "answer": "$_GET holds query string values.",
  "options": ["$_GET", "$GET", "_GET", "GET$"]
}


### 8. Add a correct MCQ -> expect 201 "Question added"
# @name newMcq
POST {{baseUrl}}/admin/questions
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "language": "{{phpId}}",
  "type": "mcq",
  "question": "TEST (IPP-402): Which one is a PHP superglobal?",
  "answer": "$_GET holds the values from the URL query string.",
  "options": ["$_GET", "$GET", "_GET", "GET$"],
  "correctOption": 0,
  "difficulty": "easy"
}


### 9. Get the MCQ with full details -> expect 200, language shows name + slug
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/questions/{{mcqId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}


### 10. Mark the Q&A as free -> expect 200, isFree true
PUT {{baseUrl}}/admin/questions/{{qaId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "isFree": true
}


### 11. Try to change the type -> expect 400 "Question type cannot be changed..."
PUT {{baseUrl}}/admin/questions/{{qaId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "mcq"
}


### 12. Edit the MCQ: new correct option + deactivate -> expect 200, correctOption 2, isActive false
PUT {{baseUrl}}/admin/questions/{{mcqId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "correctOption": 2,
  "isActive": false
}


### 13. Public languages list -> PHP still shows qaCount 21 (the test Q&A), mcqCount 20 (test MCQ is inactive)
GET {{baseUrl}}/languages/php


### 14. Delete the test Q&A -> expect 200 "Question deleted"
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/admin/questions/{{qaId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}


### 15. Delete the test MCQ -> expect 200 (no quiz has used it yet)
###     After IPP-501, an MCQ that appeared in a quiz gives 409 "...Deactivate it instead"
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/admin/questions/{{mcqId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}


### 16. Get the deleted MCQ -> expect 404 "Question not found"
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/questions/{{mcqId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}


### 17. PHP counts are back to 20 / 20 / 5
GET {{baseUrl}}/languages/php
